(::) 42 
:: 42 
:: [42]

({x*x}; neg) 
({x*x}; neg) [0]
({x*x}; neg) [1]
({x*x}; neg) [0; 5] /   *****   how to choose a function from a list/dictionary and then also run it with the next value
({x*x}; neg) [1; 5]
({x*x}; neg) [; 5] / run all functions in the list

/each both
(1,2)~1,'2 /1b ==> no effect when arguments are atoms
1,'10 20 30 /extend an atom to match a list
10 20 30,'1 /append 1 the opposite way as previous
/ can also use in prefix form
,'[("Hare Krishna Hare";"Hare Rama");(" Krishna Krishna Krishna Hare Hare";" Hare Rama Rama Rama Hare Hare")]